{"connection_id": "BC-19e524fe3d7266039502", "ref": "WLC:Zech.13.1", "target": "sec2", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "fountain opened for cleansing", "note": "The commentary's well is cleared of mud until its water appears clean; Zechariah's opened fountain cleanses sin and impurity, turning clear water into a specific image of moral purification."}
